QUTEBROWSER WORKSPACE

- [x] Make browser, terminal, and filesystem first-class tab types in the same qutebrowser window
- [x] Keep browser tabs as the default tab/content type
- [x] Add native terminal/shell tabs usable for interactive programs such as nvim
- [x] Add native cross-platform filesystem-manager tabs for Linux, Windows, and macOS
- [x] Make all three tab types work with normal tab actions: focus, close, move, duplicate where applicable, and session restore where safe

COMMANDS

- [x] Keep stock :open unchanged for normal qutebrowser browser navigation
- [x] Add independent :browser, :terminal, and :filesystem commands
- [x] Support the same placement flags on all three commands:
      -t  open a foreground tab
      -b  open a background tab
      -v  with -t, split side-by-side using a vertical divider
      -h  with -t, split stacked using a horizontal divider
- [x] Reject invalid combinations cleanly: -t/-b, -v/-h, and split flags without -t
- [x] Replace the current tab when no placement flag is supplied
- [x] Preserve filesystem-to-terminal cwd inheritance when :terminal has no explicit cwd

SPLITS

- [x] Add vertical and horizontal pane splitting inside a qutebrowser window
- [x] Allow every pane to contain browser, terminal, or filesystem tabs
- [x] Allow mixed layouts, e.g. browser + terminal or filesystem + browser
- [x] Keep panes integrated with existing qutebrowser focus and command handling
- [x] Add pane focus, close, resize, and move commands
- [x] Preserve pane layout in sessions where possible
- [x] Route :browser/:terminal/:filesystem split placement through PaneManager.split_active()

TERMINAL

- [x] Use the platform's real shell and PTY/ConPTY backend
- [x] Linux/macOS: PTY-based shell sessions
- [x] Windows: ConPTY-based shell sessions
- [x] Support interactive TUI applications, colors, resize, mouse input, clipboard, and UTF-8
- [x] Inherit qutebrowser working directory/environment sensibly

FILESYSTEM

- [x] Native keyboard-driven file manager tab
- [x] Cross-platform path, drive, volume, symlink, and permission handling
- [x] Open files/directories into appropriate qutebrowser workspace tabs/actions
- [x] Integrate filesystem cwd with terminal tabs

ARCHITECTURE

- [x] Introduce a generic workspace/tab-content abstraction instead of assuming every tab is a web page
- [x] Keep existing browser-tab implementation behind a browser content adapter
- [x] Add terminal and filesystem content adapters without embedding them in web pages
- [x] Build pane/split management above the content abstraction
- [x] Keep existing qutebrowser behavior unchanged when workspace features are unused
- [x] Add unit/integration tests for commands, tab types, pane lifecycle, session handling, and all three operating systems
